About BOCI



As a leading investment bank in China and Hong Kong region, the investment banking arm of Bank of China, BOC International Holdings Limited (“BOCI”), is now seeking highly motivated, creative and success\\-oriented professional who would like to pursue the career for supporting our group.

**Position Summary** 










 Investment Strategists under the Investment Strategy Section (ISS) are responsible for formulating asset allocation strategy, preparing periodical investment\\-related publications to drive investment\\-related activities for Private Banking, Personal Banking, and Corporate Banking customers. The Senior Investment Strategist works closely with Product Specialists of different asset classes at Investment Products and Advisory Department (IPAD) to get updated trade ideas and product information. He/she works hand\\-in\\-hand with other business partners and internal stakeholders, including but not limited to the Bank’s Economic and Research Department and BEA Union Asset Management, to develop appropriate asset allocation solutions on a timely basis. The Senior Investment Strategist also serves as a regular spokesperson with the media about BEA’s asset allocation strategies and other investment\\-related matters.










**Responsibilities** 









* Assist the Chief Investment Strategist in achieving revenue target of the Department and the Bank by driving fee income from investment products.
* Develop a House View on various asset classes (equity, fixed income, alternatives, FX), regions (developed, developing markets) and across industry sectors;
* Contribute to bilingual (English and Chinese) investment content and prepare investment publications;
* Work closely with business partners that include the Bank’s Economic and Research Department and BEA Union Asset Management in order to formulate a comprehensive investment view for the Bank;
* Communicate investment views to internal stakeholders, Relationship Managers and Clients;
* Attend selective client meetings along with Relationship Managers to discuss macroeconomic views and to follow up on Client requests;
* Attend and communicate strategy views during morning sales meetings, team meetings, product development meetings;
* Build BEA brand awareness in local and international media;
* Present investment views in media and conferences and demonstrate compelling thought leadership.
* Prepare periodical investment publications to drive investment\\-related activities of Private Banking, Personal Banking, and Corporate Banking Clients;
* Build model advisory portfolios for different client profiles with suggested asset allocation;
* Maintain model advisory portfolios based on changing market conditions and inform stakeholders of changes recommended;
* Generate short and longer\\-term investment themes that are relevant to Clients and present corresponding investment ideas to Relationship Managers and Clients by working closely with Product Specialists;
* Prepare daily market commentaries, news flashes and client\\-facing investment thought pieces;
* Other jobs and duties as assigned by the Chief Investment Strategist.









**Requirements** 









* University graduate, preferably major in economic, finance, or relevant professional qualification.
* At least 10 years of relevant working experience.
* CFA is preferred.
* Passed HKSI Paper 1, 7, 8\\.
* HKIB qualification is an advantage.
* Solid managerial experience of 5 years, preferably at a similar background.
* Sound knowledge of investment and financial products. Knowledge of FX is a must.
* Knowledge of relevant rules and regulations.
* Strong presentation, public\\-speaking and interpersonal skills with experience of facing the media and handling difficult questions.
* Knowledge of Bloomberg and Reuters will be advantageous.
* Good spoken and written English, Chinese and fluent Mandarin being an advantage.









**Other Information** 










 This position is subject to the Mandatory Reference Checking (MRC) Scheme which is implemented by the Hong Kong Monetary Authority (HKMA). In the event of BEA proceeding with a potential offer, you are obligated to give consent for the bank to conduct reference checks with your previous employers as part of the final assessment of your suitability for this role. For more details, please visit The Hong Kong Association of Banks (HKAB)’s website under the Industry Guidelines for FAQs regarding In\\-Scope Individuals in the MRC Scheme (https://www.hkab.org.hk/en/page/5/mandatory\\-reference\\-checking\\-scheme\\-phase\\-2\\). Further information can also be provided on request.










 Personal data provided by job applicants will be used for recruitment purposes only and will be treated in accordance with the Bank's Personal Information Collection (Employees) Statement and Privacy Policy Statement. Applicants who are not invited for interviews within six weeks may consider their applications unsuccessful and the personal data collected will be destroyed after 1 year.

Key Accountabilities









* Responsible for the design and execution of Hong Kong capital market projects, including but not limited to private placements, Hong Kong IPOs, placements, rights issues, and mergers and acquisitions involving Hong Kong listed companies;
* Cooperate with the global Coverage center, various sector teams and various product departments to provide support for customer marketing;
* Organize and arrange business capability improvement plans for investment banking department employees, and enhance employees' understanding of the industry, products and regulatory policies through training and other means.









 Skills \\& Experience









* Signing Principal Qualification under SFC;
* Bachelor or Master degree holders in Finance, Business or Economics from reputable universities;
* At least 8 years of relevant experience in investment banking;
* Good analytical and quantitative skills: Team player with good communication skills;
* Fluent in written and spoken English and Chinese including Putonghua.









 Other Information









* Please apply in strict confidence with full resume, academic record, current and expected salaries;
* The personal data provided will be used for consideration of recruitment only. All personal data of unsuccessful candidate will be destroyed within 24 months;
* Candidates with Enhanced Competency Framework (ECF): please state on the CV.









 About BOCI










 As a leading investment bank in China and Hong Kong region, the investment banking arm of Bank of China, BOC International Holdings Limited (“BOCI”), is now seeking highly motivated, creative and success\\-oriented professional who would like to pursue the career for supporting our group.
